it. The source of every one is at the address given, at the revision named.


Embedded in every byj binary
----------------------------

jolt, the runtime
  https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt
  Copyright (c) Dmitri Sotnikov and contributors
  Eclipse Public License 2.0
  A byj binary is a jolt binary: it embeds jolt's runtime and the works jolt
  embeds in every binary it builds — Chez Scheme (Apache License 2.0), zlib,
  LZ4 (BSD 2-Clause), irregex (BSD-style), babashka.fs and babashka.process
  (EPL 1.0), babashka.cli (MIT), and code adapted from Clojure, ClojureScript
  and others (EPL 1.0). jolt's NOTICE, in its repository and beside every
  jolt install, lists them in full with their copyrights. A release is
  built on the jolt dev/jolt-verified.edn names.


